; A sequence compares with a number element by element, and a value
; expression evaluates `a > b` as `b < a`.  So an element that cannot be
; compared with the number is reported as the `<` comparison that was
; made: `("a", 1) > 0` asks whether 0 is less than "a".

test eval '("a", 1) > 0' -> 1
__ERROR__
While evaluating value expression:
  (("a", 1) > 0)
  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
While comparing if 0 is less than a:
Error: Cannot compare an amount to a string
end test

test eval '("a", 1) < 0' -> 1
__ERROR__
While evaluating value expression:
  (("a", 1) < 0)
  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
While comparing if a is less than 0:
Error: Cannot compare a string to an amount
end test
